From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz Sobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:50:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: coda: give the SG2000 SRAM to the H.264 core per
 command

The SG2000 H.264 and H.265 cores share one SRAM, and a control register
gives it to one of them. The H.265 driver takes it for each picture.
Give it back to the H.264 core before each H.264 command, not only at
boot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Lukasz Sobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/chips-media/coda/coda-bit.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/coda/coda-bit.c b/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/coda/coda-bit.c
index 94fba2d..90d138d 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/coda/coda-bit.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/coda/coda-bit.c
@@ -85,6 +85,11 @@ static void coda_command_async(struct coda_ctx *ctx, int cmd)
 		coda_write(dev, 0, CODA9_GDI_WPROT_RGN_EN);
 	}
 
+	/* The SG2000 H.265 encoder may have taken the shared SRAM */
+	if (dev->ctrl_base)
+		writel(SG2000_VC_SRAM_TO_H264,
+		       dev->ctrl_base + SG2000_VC_SRAM_SHARE);
+
 	coda_write(dev, CODA_REG_BIT_BUSY_FLAG, CODA_REG_BIT_BUSY);
 
 	coda_write(dev, ctx->idx, CODA_REG_BIT_RUN_INDEX);
